From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] 50 px taller in portrait without automatic scaling

With scaling=[] (no automatic scaling), the keyboard keeps the base
height in both orientations.  The automatic portrait height (40 mm, 352
px on the Pro¹x) was too tall and the base 200 px a little short: in
portrait, without automatic scaling, use the base height plus 50 px.
---
--- a/src/pos-size-manager.c
+++ b/src/pos-size-manager.c
@@ -90,8 +90,10 @@
   if (!output)
     return osk_height;
 
-  if (!flags)
-    return osk_height;
+  if (!flags) {
+    /* Pro¹x: a little taller in portrait (author, 2026-11-01). */
+    return pos_output_is_portrait (output) ? osk_height + 50 : osk_height;
+  }
 
   screen_logical_height = pos_output_get_logical_height (output);
   screen_physical_height = pos_output_get_transformed_phys_height (output);
